# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# mkspeech.py - WHAT THE GAME SAYS, and the only place it is written
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `python tools/mkspeech.py` emits src/speech.inc: one phoneme string per spoken
# message plus SPK_LO/SPK_HI, the pointer table indexed by the IM_* id. The .inc
# is regenerated by `make` and tracked, so a diff of it is a diff of the voice -
# but EDIT THIS FILE, never the .inc.
#
# WHY A GENERATOR AT ALL. The bytes are %SSPPPPPP - a phoneme index in the low
# six bits, length and stress in the top two - and the table below is the English
# beside them. Hand-written .byte lines would be the same information with the
# English in a comment that nothing keeps honest.
#
# THE ORDER IS THE ABI. MESSAGES has one entry per IM_* id, IN ID ORDER
# (hud_game.s), because SPK_LO/SPK_HI are indexed by that id exactly as
# IND_LO/IND_HI are. A message with no phonemes is SILENT and gets a $00 pointer:
# the bar shows it and nothing is said. src/speech.s asserts the count against
# IM_COUNT, so adding an id without coming here is a build error, not a mystery.
#
# WRITING AN UTTERANCE. One tuple per phoneme: (phoneme, stress, comment).
#
#   * A DIPHTHONG IS TWO VOWELS. /eI/ (gATE) is EH then I, /aI/ (acquIred) is AA
#     then I, /oU/ (OPen) is AO then UH.
#   * EVERY STOP IS A CLOSURE AND THEN A BURST: CLS before P/T/K, CLZ before
#     B/D/G. Leave the silence out and /t/ is a click, not a T. The formants keep
#     gliding through the closure, so the burst already sits at the locus of the
#     vowel behind it - which is most of what tells /d/ from /k/.
#   * PAU is the gap between words, and it is not optional: without it
#     "LASER ACQUIRED" is one word.
#   * X (SHORT) is for an unstressed syllable, S (STRESS) for the one the word
#     leans on, L (LONG) for a final consonant that would otherwise clip.
#
# THE TEXT MUST BE WHAT IS ON SCREEN. Speech reduced to three squares is
# recognisable, not decodable cold: the prototype was accepted on the condition
# that the words are displayed while they are spoken (MAD-65 carts/speech_test).
# The `text` field here is the message as hud_game.s / shield.s / gate.s /
# pickup.s display it. Nothing checks that copy - so when a message's wording
# changes, its phonemes change in the same commit.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
import os

